    "updated_at": "2021-05-13T19:53:32Z",
    "body": "OK, so my reading of your first test case in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6680 is that browsers do not rewrite `/c` (in my example) to `/a`. But, they do like to tag fragments back on somehow, even if those fragments were originally for another URL!\r\n\r\nI see a couple options here:\r\n\r\n- Delay all action on this problem until the session history rewrite lands. It's the only way to be safe.\r\n\r\n- Delete the line \"Set newDocument's URL to entry's URL.\" since it mostly doesn't apply. Instead replace it with an XXX box saying something like \"It appears fragments from the entry's URL are often grafted onto newDocument's URL; see https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6680.\" Or maybe just spec that fragment-grafting.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?",
